course: dictionary
lesson: 2600
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Deploy» is one of these words, so you need the clues around it to know which meaning the writer means. Read the whole sentence first.
explain: «Letters, video calls and a calendar help when a parent works far away or is deployed (sent away to work) in the military.» The clues are far away and the military, so deployed means sent away to a place. The brackets even give you the meaning.
explain: In a crash, «the airbag deployed» means it opened out fast to protect you. In coding, to deploy a program means to put it where people can use it. The words around deploy show you which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «sent away» makes sense in the military sentence and «opened out» makes sense for the airbag, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Deploy is a verb: deploy, deploys, deployed, deploying.
fact: To deploy soldiers, ships or equipment means to send them to a place, ready to be used.
fact: To deploy something means to open it out or put it into action, like an airbag or a parachute.
fact: In computing, to deploy a program or website means to put it where people can use it.
fact: «Deployed» in the example sentence means sent away to work in the military.
exercise: «The army will deploy troops to the flooded town.» What does deploy mean here? | To sink them under the water | Packed away in a box | *To send them to a place, ready to be used | To paint them green
exercise: «The parachute deployed and the skydiver floated gently down.» What does deployed mean? | Packed away | Lost | *Opened out | Cut into pieces
exercise: Ella wants to deploy her coding game so her friends can play it. What does deploy mean here? | Hide it from the computer | Delete it forever | Make it bigger | *Put it where people can use it
test: «The rescue team will deploy a helicopter to the mountain.» What does deploy mean? | *Send the helicopter to a place, ready to be used | Park the helicopter in a garage | Close the helicopter down | Paint the helicopter
test: «The airbags deployed in the crash, protecting the driver.» What does deployed mean? | Broke into small pieces | Lost in the crash | *Opened out quickly to protect | Put away in a drawer
exam: Which sentence uses deploy to mean send to a place? | Mum deployed a cake onto the table | *The navy deployed two ships to the coast | The app was deployed in the bin | The parachute deployed above the field
